<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Get started — CSuiteFinder</title>
<meta name="description" content="Resolve a name and a company domain to a work email. Deliverability, enrichment, patterns and company data. <%= @trial_tokens %> free tokens to start.">
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #fbfaf8;
    --surface: #ffffff;
    --border: #e4e0d9;
    --text: #1c1a17;
    --muted: #6b6560;
    --accent: #b8541f;
    --accent-soft: #fdf1e8;
    --code-bg: #f5f2ee;
    --ok: #2f6b45;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root {
      --bg: #161513;
      --surface: #1e1d1a;
      --border: #33302b;
      --text: #ece8e2;
      --muted: #a09990;
      --accent: #e8834a;
      --accent-soft: #2a1d14;
      --code-bg: #131210;
      --ok: #7bbd93;
    }
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--text);
    font: 16px/1.65 ui-sans-serif, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Inter, system-ui, sans-serif;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
  }
  .wrap { max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 24px; }
  header { padding: 72px 0 40px; }
  .logo {
    font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em; font-size: 15px;
    text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent); margin-bottom: 28px;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(32px, 6vw, 52px); line-height: 1.08;
    letter-spacing: -0.03em; margin: 0 0 20px; font-weight: 700;
  }
  .lede { font-size: clamp(17px, 2.4vw, 20px); color: var(--muted); max-width: 62ch; margin: 0 0 32px; }
  h2 { font-size: 17px; margin: 28px 0 8px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  h3 {
    font-size: 13px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.09em;
    color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; margin: 64px 0 20px;
    padding-bottom: 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  p { margin: 0 0 16px; }
  a { color: var(--accent); }
  code {
    font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 0.88em; background: var(--code-bg);
    padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px;
  }
  pre {
    background: var(--code-bg); border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 10px; padding: 18px 20px; overflow-x: auto;
    font-family: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, monospace;
    font-size: 13.5px; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0 0 20px;
  }
  pre code { background: none; padding: 0; font-size: inherit; }
  .step {
    display: flex; gap: 16px; align-items: baseline;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .step-n {
    flex: none; width: 26px; height: 26px; border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent-soft); color: var(--accent);
    display: grid; place-items: center; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700;
    position: relative; top: 4px;
  }
  .cards { display: grid; gap: 14px; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(220px, 1fr)); margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .card {
    background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: 12px; padding: 20px;
  }
  .card .big { font-size: 27px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: -0.02em; display: block; }
  .card .label { font-size: 13px; color: var(--muted); }
  .table-scroll { overflow-x: auto; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: 14.5px; min-width: 480px; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: 11px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); }
  th { font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.06em; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; }
  td code { white-space: nowrap; }
  .num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }
  .note {
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); background: var(--accent-soft);
    padding: 14px 18px; border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; margin: 0 0 20px;
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  .note strong { color: var(--accent); }
  ul { margin: 0 0 16px; padding-left: 22px; }
  li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
  footer {
    margin-top: 72px; padding: 28px 0 56px;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--muted); font-size: 14px;
  }

  /* --- audience-led sections ------------------------------------------- */
  /* The base h2/h3 rules in this sheet carry visual roles rather than
     hierarchy, so section and card headings name their look explicitly.
     That keeps the document outline correct without restyling the sheet. */
  .section-label{font-size:13px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.09em;
    color:var(--muted);font-weight:600;margin:56px 0 18px;padding-bottom:10px;
    border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}
  .card-title{font-size:16.5px;text-transform:none;letter-spacing:-.01em;
    color:var(--text);font-weight:700;margin:0 0 6px;padding:0;border:none}
  .sub-label{font-size:17px;text-transform:none;letter-spacing:-.01em;
    color:var(--text);font-weight:700;margin:30px 0 10px;padding:0;border:none}
  .hero-cta{display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;align-items:center;margin:0 0 14px}
  .btn{display:inline-block;padding:13px 22px;border-radius:9px;font-weight:600;
       text-decoration:none;font-size:15.5px;border:1px solid transparent}
  .btn-primary{background:var(--accent);color:#fff}
  .btn-primary:hover{filter:brightness(1.07)}
  .btn-ghost{border-color:var(--border);color:var(--text);background:var(--surface)}
  .btn-ghost:hover{border-color:var(--accent);color:var(--accent)}
  .cta-note{font-size:13.5px;color:var(--faint)}
  .who{display:grid;gap:14px;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(230px,1fr))}
  .who .card p{margin:0;font-size:14.5px;color:var(--muted)}
  .who .card .tag{display:inline-block;font-size:11px;text-transform:uppercase;
    letter-spacing:.07em;font-weight:700;color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:9px}
  .does{display:grid;gap:0;margin-bottom:18px}
  .does .item{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(180px,1fr) 2fr;gap:18px;
    padding:15px 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);align-items:baseline}
  .does .item:last-child{border-bottom:none}
  .does .item strong{font-size:15.5px}
  .does .item span{color:var(--muted);font-size:14.5px}
  @media (max-width:620px){.does .item{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:4px}}
  .bundle-grid{display:grid;gap:12px;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(190px,1fr));
    margin-bottom:14px}
  .bundle-card{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:12px;
    padding:20px;position:relative}
  .bundle-card.best{border-color:var(--accent)}
  .bundle-card .amt{font-size:27px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.02em;display:block}
  .bundle-card .qty{font-size:14px;color:var(--text);margin-top:4px;display:block}
  .bundle-card .rate{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--faint);margin-top:8px;display:block}
  .bundle-card .flag{position:absolute;top:-9px;right:14px;background:var(--accent);color:#fff;
    font-size:10.5px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;
    padding:3px 9px;border-radius:99px}
  .dev{border-top:1px solid var(--border);margin-top:56px;padding-top:8px}
  .quiet{color:var(--muted);font-size:14.5px}

  .big-step{display:grid;grid-template-columns:44px 1fr;gap:18px;margin-bottom:30px;align-items:start}
  .big-step .n{width:38px;height:38px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--accent);color:#fff;
    display:grid;place-items:center;font-weight:700;font-size:16px}
  .big-step h3{margin:6px 0 8px;font-size:19px;text-transform:none;letter-spacing:-.015em;
    color:var(--text);font-weight:700;padding:0;border:none}
  .big-step p{margin:0 0 12px;color:var(--muted)}
  .copyblock{position:relative}
  /* A block whose whole purpose is to be copied should be readable at a glance,
     so it wraps rather than scrolling sideways. The right padding keeps text
     from running under the copy button. */
  .copyblock pre{margin:0;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;padding-right:86px}
  .copybtn{position:absolute;top:10px;right:10px;font:inherit;font-size:12.5px;font-weight:600;
    padding:6px 12px;border-radius:6px;border:1px solid var(--border);background:var(--surface);
    color:var(--muted);cursor:pointer}
  .copybtn:hover{border-color:var(--accent);color:var(--accent)}
  .asks{display:grid;gap:12px;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(250px,1fr))}
  .ask{background:var(--surface);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:12px;padding:17px}
  .ask .who{font-size:11px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;font-weight:700;
    color:var(--accent);margin-bottom:8px;display:block}
  .ask p{margin:0;font-size:14.5px;font-style:italic;color:var(--text)}
  .timing{display:inline-block;background:var(--accent-soft);color:var(--accent);font-weight:700;
    font-size:12.5px;padding:5px 12px;border-radius:99px;margin-bottom:18px}
  .alt{border-top:1px solid var(--border);margin-top:50px;padding-top:26px}
<%= CsuiteFinderWeb.Nav.css() %></style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">

<%= CsuiteFinderWeb.Nav.render(:start) %>

<header>
  <span class="timing">About a minute</span>
  <h1>Get started</h1>
  <p class="lede">
    You do not have to read our documentation. If you use an AI assistant, one line
    tells it everything it needs — including the prices — and it takes over from there.
  </p>
</header>

<h2 class="section-label">The one-paste setup</h2>

<div class="big-step">
  <span class="n">1</span>
  <div>
    <h3>Give your assistant this line</h3>
    <p>
      Works with Claude, ChatGPT, Cursor, Copilot — anything that can read a web page
      and make a request.
    </p>
    <div class="copyblock">
      <button class="copybtn" data-copy="prompt1">Copy</button>
      <pre><code id="prompt1">Read <%= @base_url %>/llms.txt and use the CSuiteFinder API to find work email addresses for me. Register for a free key first, and verify every address before you give it to me.</code></pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="big-step">
  <span class="n">2</span>
  <div>
    <h3>It sets itself up</h3>
    <p>
      That file is written for machines. Your assistant reads it, registers an account,
      and gets <strong><%= @trial_tokens %> free lookups</strong> — no card, no form, no
      waiting for anyone to approve you. It knows every endpoint and what each one costs,
      because the file is generated from the live service.
    </p>
    <p>
      Ask it to show you the key it created, and keep a copy. We only ever store a hash of
      it, so it cannot be re-sent.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="big-step">
  <span class="n">3</span>
  <div>
    <h3>Ask for what you actually want</h3>
    <p>
      Now talk to it normally. It already knows how to chain the calls — find the address,
      check it is deliverable, tell you who it belongs to.
    </p>
    <div class="asks">
      <div class="ask">
        <span class="who">Sales</span>
        <p>"Here are 40 names and their companies. Get me verified emails for the ones that check out, and tell me which ones bounced."</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ask">
        <span class="who">Founders</span>
        <p>"Find the email for Sarah Chen at sequoiacap.com, confirm it's real, and tell me her title before I write to her."</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ask">
        <span class="who">Ops</span>
        <p>"Someone emailed me from jhuang@nvidia.com — who are they and what does the company do?"</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="note">
  <strong>Tell your assistant one thing up front:</strong> this finds the address of someone
  you can already name. It is not a prospect database and will not build your list. Bring the
  names — from LinkedIn, a conference programme, a company's about page — and it does the rest.
</div>

<h2 class="section-label">Make it permanent</h2>

<p class="quiet">
  If your assistant remembers project instructions, put this line in them — in Claude's
  <code>CLAUDE.md</code>, an <code>AGENTS.md</code>, Cursor rules, or a custom GPT's
  instructions — and it will keep the API to hand without being told again:
</p>

<div class="copyblock">
  <button class="copybtn" data-copy="prompt2">Copy</button>
  <pre><code id="prompt2">For work email lookups, use the CSuiteFinder API documented at <%= @base_url %>/llms.txt. The key is in the CSF_API_KEY environment variable.</code></pre>
</div>

<div class="alt">
<h2 class="section-label">No assistant? Two other ways</h2>

<h3 class="sub-label">In your browser</h3>
<p class="quiet">
  <a href="/account"><strong>Open your account</strong></a>, enter your email, and you have a key
  and <%= @trial_tokens %> lookups. The same page shows your balance, your usage and lets you buy
  more — no headers, no terminal.
</p>

<h3 class="sub-label">From the command line</h3>
<div class="copyblock">
  <button class="copybtn" data-copy="prompt3">Copy</button>
  <pre><code id="prompt3">KEY=$(curl -s -X POST <%= @base_url %>/csuitefinder/register \
  -H 'content-type: application/json' \
  -d '{"email":"you@company.com"}' | grep -o '"api_key":"[^"]*' | cut -d'"' -f4)

curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $KEY" \
  "<%= @base_url %>/csuitefinder/email/find?full_name=Jensen%20Huang&domain=nvidia.com"</code></pre>
</div>
<p class="quiet">
  The full reference is on the <a href="/#developers">home page</a>, and
  <a href="/llms.txt"><code>llms.txt</code></a> is readable by people too — it is just Markdown.
</p>
</div>

<h2 class="section-label">What it costs</h2>

<p class="quiet">
  Your first <strong><%= @trial_tokens %> lookups are free</strong> (<%= @trial_usd %> of credit) —
  real lookups, not a limited preview. After that you pay <strong>one token per email found</strong>
  at $<%= @token_price %>, and nothing at all for deliverability checks, identity lookups, company
  data or email formats. A lookup that finds nothing is free.
</p>

<p style="margin-top:22px">
  <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/account">Create your free account</a>
  <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/llms.txt">Read llms.txt</a>
</p>

<footer>
  <a href="/">Home</a> ·
  <a href="/account">Your account</a> ·
  <a href="/llms.txt">llms.txt</a> ·
  <a href="/csuitefinder/health">status</a>
</footer>

</div>

<script>
document.querySelectorAll(".copybtn").forEach(function (btn) {
  btn.addEventListener("click", function () {
    var text = document.getElementById(btn.getAttribute("data-copy")).textContent;
    navigator.clipboard.writeText(text).then(function () {
      btn.textContent = "Copied";
      setTimeout(function () { btn.textContent = "Copy"; }, 1600);
    }, function () {
      btn.textContent = "Select it manually";
    });
  });
});
</script>
</body>
</html>
